# Krishi Mitr — web deployment environment.
#
# Copy the NAMES from here into Vercel → Project Settings → Environment
# Variables. Never put a real value in this file: it is committed, and a key
# that reaches git history stays there even after the line is deleted (I10).
# A leaked key gets rotated, not erased.

# Sarvam AI keys for the voice, as a comma-separated pool.
#
#   SARVAM_API_KEYS=sk_xxxxxxxx_aaaaaaaaaaaa,sk_yyyyyyyy_bbbbbbbbbbbb
#
# Both voice functions walk this list in order and move to the next key on
# 401 / 402 / 403 / 429 — the statuses that mean "this key is out of credit,
# revoked, or throttled" rather than "this request is bad". One key is enough
# to work; two is what stops a demo dying when the first runs out of credit
# mid-sentence, which has already happened to this project once.
#
# ★ Use keys that are NOT the ones in the mobile backend's .env. If the phone
#   and the website share a pool, a judge exercising the website drains the
#   credit the phone demo needs, and neither team can tell whose requests
#   spent it.
SARVAM_API_KEYS=

# Optional: a single key is also accepted, for convenience.
# SARVAM_API_KEY=
